Brown here in North Carolina

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.360
and seeing the way that my
students are bearing the weight

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.000
of that and feeling that

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.300
and on top of having an ongoing pandemic,

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.030
it just feels like a
really challenging season.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.440
So I'm both grateful and also just aware

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.393
of how much is going on all around us.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:12.197
- Yeah, that makes a lot
of sense in a lot of ways

00:10:12.197 --> 00:10:14.410
and definitely appreciate your
awareness of that as well.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:15.430
I mean, you're leading off talking

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.590
about, I imagine you do this
with your students as well

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:18.820
but your own tiredness,

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.990
so not to ignore that but to acknowledge

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.740
and I think all of us have
done that and acknowledged,

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.810
I mean, clearly some
having gone through COVID

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.910
as Pastor Mike mentioned

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:30.910
and Dr. Green also mentioned
some of the health challenges,

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.890
just the reality of what
